			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync Element submodules with upstream fixes\n\nSynchronize the Element submodule to caa2b47f, bringing multiple downstream updates:\n- Mountain: Fix duplicate DevTools window in debug builds by removing redundant open_devtools() call from WindowBuild.rs, update DiagnosticProvider docstring to clarify 1-based indexing\n- Output: Disable PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration transform due to \"black shadow over text\" artifacts in WKWebView, add ViewRegistrySnapshot() to __CEL_SERVICES__ facade\n- Sky: Add reentrancy guard (_SkyBridgeInstalled, _SkyBridgeInstallPromise) to prevent duplicate Tauri listen() registrations causing double-render \"purple overlays\" bug, update astro.config.ts with static output and disabled prerendering\n- Cocoon: Submodule sync bringing cross-cutting synchronizations\n\nThis synchronization brings in the reentrancy guard fix for the workbench loading twice issue, disables the GPU acceleration transform that introduced visual artifacts, and removes the duplicate DevTools window opening behavior.",
			"SHA": "02d2e32fffdabcfccc45d1d45b5e13040d5f0800"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:43:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Complete terminal race-condition fix via submodule sync\n\nSynchronize Element submodules to complete the terminal race-condition fix cycle:\n- Mountain: Complete the terminal race-condition fix by deferring the `sky://terminal/create` event with a 120ms delay. This addresses the timing vulnerability where the Tauri event arrived before `_ptys.set(id, pty)` completed during step 1 (RPC in-flight), causing `_ptys.get(id)` to return undefined and silently dropping keystrokes. Complements the earlier fix that added the `AppendTerminalOutput` replay buffer for data events.\n- Output: Add disabled `PatchTerminalGpuAcceleration` transform that defaults `terminal.integrated.gpuAcceleration` to `'off'` to work around xterm.js WebGL texture atlas font drift in WKWebView.\n- Cocoon: Submodule sync to latest.\n\nThis synchronization completes the terminal race-condition fix cycle that began with bf94e30, restoring proper terminal panel functionality.",
			"SHA": "e1f9361be392209a7f4b7fed12867c22a908204e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:20:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Sync submodules bringing Mountain terminalPTY fix\n\nSynchronize Element and Dependency submodules to bring in the critical Mountain fix (c99ccbe7) for blank terminal panels. The VS Code terminal workbench expects `IPtyService.createProcess` to return a `Promise<number>` (the integer terminal id), but Mountain was incorrectly returning the full `{id, name, pid}` object. This caused the workbench's `_ptys` map lookups to fail, resulting in xterm receiving zero bytes despite data being emitted continuously.\n\nThe fix splits the terminal handler into three paths: spawn preserves full response for Cocoon's Sky bridge, createProcess returns only the integer id per VS Code contract, and start is a no-op for the eager-spawn pattern.\n\nAlso brings Dependency CHANGELOG update (cb1f22c0) documenting version history.\n\nResolves terminal panel blank display issue in the editor workbench.",
			"SHA": "4fc8e7994bb05c1cea96ae0774573f4dde362b94"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:00:42Z",
